{
 "title": "Autoencoder (8×8 digits)",
 "description": "A plain autoencoder for scikit-learn's 8×8 handwritten digits, the model in the lecture \"Generative AI: learn the distribution, then sample\". The encoder (64 → 128 → 64 → 2, ReLU) squeezes each image into a 2-number code z; the decoder (2 → 64 → 128 → 64, ReLU) gives pixel logits. There are no labels: the target is the input itself, and the loss is binary cross-entropy summed over the 64 pixels (64 × the mean). predict() applies the sigmoid. Compare with VAE (8×8 digits), which differs only in its code. 33,474 parameters.",
